{"uid":"481c59adaa001af4","name":"test_delivery_refuses_to_follow_a_redirect_to_another_host","fullName":"tests.test_events_webhooks#test_delivery_refuses_to_follow_a_redirect_to_another_host","historyId":"fde1655d94c99f04270e41204024922d","time":{"start":1785657419306,"stop":1785657419810,"duration":504},"description":"The receiver must not get to choose where CALIBER sends the signature.\n\n    ``urlopen`` installs the default opener, which follows redirects, so an\n    operator-configured URL became a URL the *receiver* selects. Measured\n    against this exact pair of servers before the fix: the 302 was followed and\n    the second host received ``X-Caliber-Signature`` and ``X-Caliber-Timestamp``\n    intact. urllib rewrites POST to GET on a 302 so the body was dropped — but a\n    valid HMAC for that payload had already reached a host the operator never\n    configured, which is the disclosure that matters.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The receiver must not get to choose where CALIBER sends the signature.</p>\n<pre><code>``urlopen`` installs the default opener, which follows redirects, so an\noperator-configured URL became a URL the *receiver* selects. Measured\nagainst this exact pair of servers before the fix: the 302 was followed and\nthe second host received ``X-Caliber-Signature`` and ``X-Caliber-Timestamp``\nintact. urllib rewrites POST to GET on a 302 so the body was dropped — but a\nvalid HMAC for that payload had already reached a host the operator never\nconfigured, which is the disclosure that matters.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1785656695595,"stop":1785656695595,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_clear_prompt_info_